                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Despite suffering from many of the same flaws as Act I, Act II is a step in the right direction and does a number of things better than the first game. The animations are as clunky as before, and some of the puzzles are completely lacking in terms of any logic, but I felt that overall, the game felt better paced and with more of an actual structure - also thanks to the better storytelling. \n\nWrath also fleshes out the character of Silvia, and the bits with her were definitely enjoyable. It was nice to also have some real-time puzzling in the very beginning, which also contributed to the overall atmosphere. Beyond the usual object combinations, there were also some nice puzzles here and there: such as the phone call analysis and map plotting, as well as the final puzzle with the roman numerals. Not great, but definitely much better than the majority of puzzles in Act I.\n\nPerhaps what improved my experience this time around was my decision to play with Italian voice acting in order to bypass the atrocious voice acting in English. This was a wise choice, as the Italian actors do a much better job. On the whole, I still wouldn't recommend this game to anyone except fans of the genre. However, with Act III seemingly not being very far off, I am reasonably excited and hopeful that this can turn into the game that it deserves to be.",
